PVD("brunei_ndp_2018-2023",{"docs":["","BRU NDP 2018 2023"],"s":{"1":[[1,"53","13","RKN Project Management System Monitoring Update","Ensured the monitoring system, RKN Project Management System (RKNPMS) was fully used and updated by the client and implementing agency;",""],[1,"53","15","Project Site Monitoring Visits","Organised scheduled and surprise visits to project sites to ensure the physical progress met the scheduled implementation progress;",""],[1,"44","3","Wawasan Brunei 2035 Framework","Development of the Wawasan Brunei 2035 Framework to assess and measure the level of achievement and the country's progress towards Wawasan Brunei 2035 in a much clearer and detailed manner.",""],[1,"44","6","Wawasan Brunei 2035 Supreme Council Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","One of the main roles of the Wawasan Brunei 2035 Supreme Council is to assure that the three (3) main goals of Wawasan are achieved through the Wawasan Brunei 2035 Framework; by providing policy directions for the realisation of Wawasan Brunei 2035; as well as ensuring implementation of policies and strategies at the top level are aligned, integrated and sustainable.",""],[1,"44","7","Wawasan Champions Strategic Action Planning and Stakeholder Engagement Mechanism","the Wawasan Champions are responsible for identifying strategies to achieve the National Outcomes; formulating and implementing strategic action plans along with conducting engagements with relevant stakeholders between Government agencies, private sector, non-Governmental organisations and the general public in the planning process; and to ensure the implementation of high impact programmes and projects at the national level.",""],[1,"44","2","Wawasan Brunei 2035 Governing Structure","Establishment of a governing structure for Wawasan Brunei 2035, comprising of the Wawasan Brunei 2035 Supreme Council and the Wawasan Champions, to create and generate synergy towards integrated planning and achieving Wawasan Brunei 2035.",""],[1,"94","2","Periodic Review and Improvement of Ongoing Programmes","On-going programmes will be reviewed periodically to ensure their relevance and improvements would be implemented so as to enhance the effectiveness of these programmes.",""]],"2":[[1,"53","14","Value-for-Money Public Construction Spending","The planned expenditure will be based on the average rates for the costs of construction of Government buildings and projects to ensure projects are not over-specified and exceed their actual functions or needs;",""],[1,"63","1","Fiscal Consolidation Efforts","the Government has stepped up fiscal consolidation efforts to control Government expenditure and increase revenue.",""],[1,"97","2","Public Expenditure Efficiency Improvement","the Government will continue to improve the effectiveness and efficiency of expenditure without compromising the quality of service delivery.",""],[1,"97","3","RKN Project Prioritization and Value-for-Money Appraisal","RKN projects are assessed according to priority and emphasises on 'cost-effectiveness', 'value-for-money', 'functional' needs, while taking into account the commitments to maintenance and yearly operation expenditure, and projected revenue.",""],[1,"97","3","Shared Public Facilities Utilization Policy","Consideration should also be taken into using shared existing facilities to control public expenditure as well as to foster solidarity among the Bruneian citizens.",""],[1,"98","1","Fiscal Stability and Prudent Spending Policy","From the Fiscal aspect, we also need to maintain our fiscal stability policy, especially in considering the fiscal allocation and expenditure of the country that emphasises on prudent spending and value for money, with such practice Insya' Allah, it can enable the country to save and use these savings to accommodate future provisions when it is more needed.",""]],"3":[[1,"61","7","E-Government ICT Application Improvement","Such efforts include improving Info-Communications Technology (ICT) application through e-Government projects, Research and Development (R&D), education, training, expertise as well as innovation;",""],[1,"112","2","Government Process Reform and Online Service Delivery","These include the reform of the traditional processes to innovative Government processes.",""],[1,"112","3","Public Service Training Strengthening Initiative","Therefore, initiatives by the Government to provide relevant trainings, will continue to be strengthened.",""],[1,"112","4","ICT Infrastructure for E-Services Expansion","In RKN11, the Government will continue to provide the necessary infrastructure including ICT facilities, to increase the capacity of e-services in supporting the efficient management of the public service.",""],[1,"113","2","Integrated E-Government System Upgrade","initiatives will be implemented include the integrated upgrading and improving of the e-Government system,",""],[1,"125","13","Online Land Payment System Phase 2","Online Land Payment System Phase 2",""],[1,"123","10","Online Housing Application and Financing Billing System","Online Housing Application and Financing Billing System",""]],"4":[[1,"76","2","Human Capital Development for Quality Education","emphasis on developing human capital is also given on achieving high quality teaching and training by committed teaching staff with relevant qualifications and skills, the utilisation of the latest technologies in learning techniques, and the provision of a conducive environment and quality educational facilities3.",""],[1,"76","4","Education Channel Expansion and Quality Improvement","In the field of education, efforts are being made in expanding the education channels while also strengthening its quality towards the achievement of Wawasan Brunei 2035.",""],[1,"77","1","National Education System Strengthening","The Government needs to ensure on-going efforts to strengthen the national education system",""],[1,"77","2","Public Examination Achievement Improvement Initiative","This thrust focuses on two (2) main objectives. The first objective focuses on improving academic achievements.",""],[1,"78","4","21st Century National Education System (SPN21)","The Government has introduced the 21st Century National Education System (SPN21).",""],[1,"78","4","Education and Training Quality Improvement","improvements will be implemented to further enhance the quality of education and training provided to the youths of Brunei Darussalam.",""],[1,"79","1","Primary and Secondary Literacy and Numeracy Improvement Initiative","efforts to improve students' academic achievements at the primary and secondary levels, particularly in literacy and numeracy, are currently being pursued.",""],[1,"80","5","ICT-Based Innovative Teaching and Learning Programme","teaching and learning through innovative education and technology are also being implemented.",""],[1,"80","6","Technical and Vocational Education System Transformation","the transformation of the Technical and Vocational Education which aims to upgrade the technical and vocational education system to be more responsive to the needs of the labour market in accordance to the demands of technological progress and national economic development.",""],[1,"93","5","Universal Primary and Secondary Education Provision","the Government will focus on learning from an early stage through the provision of primary and secondary education across the country",""]],"6":[[1,"61","7","Research and Development, Education, Training and Innovation Support","Such efforts include improving Info-Communications Technology (ICT) application through e-Government projects, Research and Development (R&D), education, training, expertise as well as innovation;",""],[1,"81","4","School Infrastructure Upgrade and Extension Programme","the approved RKN11 projects includes the upgrading and extension of existing primary, secondary and religious schools",""],[1,"93","6","Religious and Arabic School Projects","the provision of religious education will continue to be given adequate emphasis, whereby a number of Religious and Arabic school projects have been approved, in line with the enforcement of the Compulsory Religious Education Order 2012.",""],[1,"116","2","Construction of Islamic Religious Activity Centre and Religious School Building","Construction of New Building for Islamic Religious Activity Centre / Kampong Senukoh Religious School",""],[1,"116","5","Upgrading of Hassanal Bolkiah Boys Arabic Secondary School","Upgrading of Hassanal Bolkiah Boys Arabic Secondary School",""],[1,"116","6","Covered Netball Court Construction","Construction of Covered Netball Court, Raja Isteri Pengiran Anak Damit Girls Arabic Secondary School",""],[1,"116","8","New Building for Kampong Kiulap Religious School","New Building for Kampong Kiulap Religious School",""],[1,"116","9","New Building for Kampong Bolkiah Religious School","New Building for Kampong Bolkiah Religious School",""],[1,"116","11","Rebuilding of Sultan Hassan Bangar Secondary School","Rebuilding of Sultan Hassan Bangar Secondary School Temburong",""],[1,"116","12","Extension Building for Menglait Secondary School","Extension Building for Menglait Secondary School",""],[1,"116","13","Primary School Extension Building","Extension Building for Sultan Abdul Bubin Sungai Besar Primary School",""],[1,"116","14","Primary School Extension Building","Extension Building for AHMY Katimahar Primary School",""],[1,"116","15","Extension Building for Bendahara Sakam Bunut Primary School","Extension Building for Bendahara Sakam Bunut Primary School",""],[1,"116","18","Upgrading and Extension of Orang Kaya Setia Bakti Kilanas Primary School","Upgrading and Extension of Orang Kaya Setia Bakti Kilanas Primary School",""],[1,"116","19","Upgrading and Extension of Sengkurong Primary School","Upgrading and Extension of Sengkurong Primary School",""],[1,"116","25","Government School Network Infrastructure Upgrading","Upgrading Government School Network Infrastructure",""],[1,"117","1","Additional Hall and Lecture Rooms for Youth Development Centre","Additional Hall and Lecture Rooms for Youth Development Centre",""]],"7":[[1,"71","1","Education and Labour Force Skills Improvement","This will require a focus towards improving the quality of education and the skills of the labour force.",""],[1,"76","1","Education and Training Investment for Youth Skills Development","Investments in education and training will help to develop the potential of the country's youth in various fields of expertise.",""],[1,"76","1","Youth Education and Training Opportunities Expansion","The Government has provided a variety of educational and training opportunities to build the knowledge and skills of youths to meet the demands of the domestic labour market.",""],[1,"77","4","Technical and Vocational Education Quality Improvement and Diversification","The second objective focuses on efforts to diversify and improve the quality of technical and vocational education which offers a variety of courses in specific areas relevant to the needs of the country.",""],[1,"77","4","Youth Reskilling and Competency Development Programme","Better quality and relevance programmes and training will be provided to avail local youth with opportunities for reskilling, and to continuously enhance their talents and competencies.",""],[1,"78","2","Short Courses and In-Service Training for Public and Private Sector Workers","opportunities are made available by the Government for those working in the public and private sectors to further enhance their level of education and skills through various short courses and training, both locally and abroad, as well as through the in-service training programmes.",""],[1,"81","2","Scholarship and Workforce Training Programme","The Government will also continue to extend scholarship to students as well as training for employees in the public and private sectors in ensuring that the human resource pool in this country will have the highest level of education and skills in various fields, in line with the changes in economic demands.",""],[1,"81","3","Lifelong Education and Informal Skills Upgrading Programme","Informal education such as through advanced classes, special courses and others will be enhanced and programmes offered will be expanded towards the creation of a more competitive human capital pool.",""],[1,"82","3","Human Capital Development Programme","the Government will be implementing the Human Capital Development Programme in a holistic and inclusive manner, which encompasses the acquisition of knowledge and skills, including entrepreneurial capabilities, as well as the cultivation of positive attitudes, values and ethics towards socio-economic advancement through programmes which are structured, relevant and focused in the achievement of outcomes.",""],[1,"85","3","Local Manpower Development and Human Resource Preparation","The Government will spearhead the development and planning of local manpower as well as the preparation for high-quality human resources through a supportive ecosystem.",""],[1,"86","2","PPK Youth Skills and Employment Programme","PPK is one of the main initiatives as a national effort towards reducing unemployment, with a target of reducing the number of unemployed persons by around 3,000 people by the end of 2018.",""],[1,"87","1","Youth Skills Development through Industry Competency Framework Courses","My Government is also currently increasing efforts to equip youths with relevant skills.","Human Resource Unit, Prime Minister's Office | Ministry of Education"],[1,"87","2","Centre for Capacity Building Training Initiative","I have consented an additional initiative, the Centre for Capacity Building (PPK), which will offer training opportunities for local youths in order to qualify them to hold job positions in the private sector, including foreign direct investment (FDI) companies",""],[1,"87","4","Graduate Apprenticeship Scheme (i-Ready)","a Graduate Apprenticeship Scheme or 'i-Ready' has been introduced.",""],[1,"87","6","I-Ready Graduate Apprenticeship Programme","I have consented for the creation of an Apprenticeship programme specifically for graduates who are still seeking employment.",""],[1,"88","1","TVET-Industry Alignment Programme","This initiative is aimed at aligning technical and vocational training programmes with the needs of industries.",""],[1,"88","3","Incentive Scheme for Qualified Graduates","The ISQ aims to give an incentive for students who have completed their training in Registered Training Organizations (RTOs) to get employment within their field of study in the private sector.",""],[1,"88","4","Youth Training and Development Programmes","initiatives under this thrust also comprises of training and development programmes for youths of all ages, including through technical and vocational education or through related institutions such as the Youth Development Centre (PPB), the Entrepreneurship Development Centre and etc.,",""],[1,"89","1","Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme","the Government has prepared a scholarship scheme i.e. Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme (BPTV) under the RKN specifically for 'O' level graduates to further their studies in private educational institutions.",""],[1,"106","11","Industry-Focused Training Programmes","RKN11 also focuses on the implementation of 'soft infrastructure' projects such as training programmes.",""]],"8":[[1,"36","5","Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme","Biasiswa Pendidikan Teknikal dan Vokasional / Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme",""],[1,"42","5","Human Resource Development Fund and Scholarships","the related RKN11 projects includes new and additional construction of buildings and infrastructure, improvement to the national education management system in addition to the provision of human resource development fund and scholarships.",""],[1,"50","8","Human Resources Fund","This was due to the implementation of mega projects such as the 4,000 unit housing project for Kampong Mengkubau National Housing; 1,500 unit housing project for Daerah Tutong National Housing; 1,000 unit cluster houses for Kampong Lugu National Housing; and also the Human Resources Fund.",""],[1,"55","2","Human Resource Fund","These positive developments will continue to be further enhanced during the RKN11, by introducing new programmes to produce highly-skilled and educated people such as the Civil Service Leadership Pipeline (CSLP), Human Resource Fund as well as projects for building, upgrading and construction of school buildings in the country.",""]],"9":[[1,"122","1","Reforestation Programme on Degraded Forest Areas","Reforestation Programme on Degraded Forest Areas",""]],"12":[[1,"43","2","World-Class Healthcare Provision","related RKN11 projects will focus on providing a world class healthcare",""],[1,"98","6","Construction of Silver Jubilee Health Centre New Block","the construction of a new block for Silver Jubilee Health Centre at Sengkurong",""],[1,"98","6","Construction of Emergency Services Building at Suri Seri Begawan Hospital","the construction of emergency services building at Suri Seri Begawan Hospital in Kuala Belait",""],[1,"98","6","Establishment of Certified BSL3 and Supporting BSL2 Laboratories","Establishment of Certified BSL3 Laboratories with Supporting BSL2 Labs for An Accredited National TB Reference Laboratory (NTRL) and Virology Services",""],[1,"122","3","Suri Seri Hospital Emergency Services Construction","Construction of Suri Seri Hospital Emergency Services, Kuala Belait",""],[1,"122","4","Certified BSL3 and Supporting BSL2 Laboratory Establishment","Establishment of Certified BSL3 Laboratories with Supporting BSL2 Labs for an Accredited National TB Reference Laboratory (NTRL) and Virology Services",""],[1,"122","5","Construction of Pandan Health Centre","Construction of Pandan Health Centre, Belait District",""]],"13":[[1,"50","8","National Housing Projects","This was due to the implementation of mega projects such as the 4,000 unit housing project for Kampong Mengkubau National Housing; 1,500 unit housing project for Daerah Tutong National Housing; 1,000 unit cluster houses for Kampong Lugu National Housing; and also the Human Resources Fund.",""],[1,"43","2","Affordable Quality Housing Access Initiative","accessibility to good quality dwellings",""]],"14":[[1,"93","6","New Mosque Construction Projects","a number of projects for the construction of new mosques have also been approved for implementation within RKN11.",""],[1,"118","1","Kampong Mengkubau National Housing Mosque Construction","Construction of Kampong Mengkubau National Housing Mosque",""],[1,"118","2","Construction of Kampong Meragang National Housing Mosque","Construction of Kampong Meragang National Housing Mosque",""],[1,"118","3","Kampong Lugu National Housing Mosque Construction","Construction of Kampong Lugu National Housing Mosque",""],[1,"118","4","Kampong Rimba National Housing Mosque Construction","Construction of Kampong Rimba National Housing Mosque",""],[1,"118","5","Kampong Telisai Landless Indigenous Citizen Housing Scheme Mosque Construction","Construction of Kampong Telisai Landless Indigenous Citizen Housing Scheme Mosque",""],[1,"118","6","Construction of Kampong Lumut National Housing Mosque","Construction of Kampong Lumut National Housing Mosque",""]],"15":[[1,"121","15","Airport Secure Fencing and Perimeter Intruder Detection System","Secure Fencing & Perimeter Intruder Detection System in Brunei International Airport",""],[1,"121","16","Centralized Screening Equipment and Security Surveillance System Upgrade","Enhancement of Centralized Screening Equipment and Security Surveillance System for Brunei International Airport",""],[1,"121","14","Airfield Pavement Rehabilitation Works at Brunei International Airport Phase 2","Airfield Pavement Rehabilitation Works at Brunei International Airport Phase 2",""]],"16":[[1,"50","10","Industrial Development Projects and Sungai Liang Industrial Park","In addition, this sector also include the Industrial Development projects and Sungai Liang Industrial Park.",""],[1,"43","5","Key Sectors Development Projects","RKN11 projects that support the achievement of this goal include projects that enhance the development of key sectors, improving the infrastructure and basic utilities for industrial sites, rehabilitation and upgrading of tourism sites and implementation of capacity development programmes.",""],[1,"106","10","Industrial Site Basic Infrastructure Provision","the provision of basic infrastructure for industrial sites towards the development of non-oil and gas output",""],[1,"107","3","Non-Oil and Gas Sector Development Initiatives","the Government through this RKN11 will continue its effort to focus on developing the Non-Oil and Gas Sector through various initiatives comprising of development of physical infrastructure and technology, entrepreneurship, knowledge and expertise.",""],[1,"124","9","Pulau Muara Besar Phase 2 Development","Development of Pulau Muara Besar - Phase 2",""]],"17":[[1,"125","2","Additional Irrigation Scheme Construction for Paddy Planting Areas","Construction of Additional Irrigation Scheme for Paddy Planting Areas in all Districts",""],[1,"124","16","Genetic Development and Selective Breeding Programmes","Genetic Development and Selective Breeding Programmes to Increase Aquaculture Industry Productivity",""],[1,"125","5","Commercial Paddy Planting Expansion, Kandol Area","Opening of 500 Hectare Commercial Paddy Planting, Kandol Area, Belait District (2nd Phase)",""]],"18":[[1,"99","1","Public Transport and Road Infrastructure Improvement Programme","The construction / repairs of Public Transport Infrastructure that is under the improvement and repair of bridge and roads infrastructure programme as well as construction of flyover.",""],[1,"120","11","Improvement and Repair of Road Infrastructure Programme","Improvement and Repair of Road Infrastructure Programme",""],[1,"120","12","Improvement and Repair of Bridge Infrastructure Programme","Improvement and Repair of Bridge Infrastructure Programme",""],[1,"120","13","Flyover Construction at Muara-Tutong Highway Interchange and Tanjung Kajar Industrial Site","Construction of Flyover at Muara - Tutong Highway Interchange / Tanjung Kajar Industrial Site",""],[1,"120","14","Muara-Tutong Highway Flyover Construction","Construction of Flyover at Muara-Tutong Highway / Kampong Lugu Housing Junction",""],[1,"120","15","Tanah Jambu Link Road and Mengkubau Flyover Construction","Construction of Tanah Jambu Link Road and Flyover at Mengkubau National Housing Junction/Mentiri Main Road",""],[1,"120","16","Residency Road Expansion Phase II","Expansion of Residency Road (Phase II)",""],[1,"124","2","Serasa Industrial Road Upgrade","Upgrading of Serasa Industrial Road towards Pulau Muara Besar Bridge",""],[1,"124","4","Secondary Road Upgrade for Serasa Industrial Sites","Upgrading of Secondary Road for Serasa Industrial Sites",""]],"20":[[1,"120","22","Sewerage Treatment Plant and Pumping Station Upgrading","Upgrading of Gadong Phase 2, Pintu Malim Sewerage Treatment Plants and Pumping Stations",""],[1,"121","18","Sewer Pipes System Upgrading in Brunei Muara Catchment Areas","Upgrading of Sewer Pipes System at Brunei Muara Catchment Areas",""],[1,"121","19","Sewer System Upgrading in Kuala Belait and Seria Municipal Areas","Upgrading of Sewer System at Kuala Belait and Seria Municipal Areas",""]],"21":[[1,"121","13","Bukit Barun Water Treatment Plant Stage 8 Construction","Construction of Bukit Barun Water Treatment Plant Stage 8",""],[1,"121","6","Badas Raw Water Pumping Station and Pipeline Construction","Construction of Badas New Raw Water Pumping Station and Installation of Raw Water Pipeline from Badas to SPARK",""],[1,"50","10","Electrical Services and Water Supply Infrastructure Projects","Projects under this sector consisted of electrical services projects such as the Bukit Panggal Power Station, Power Generation Lumut Station Phase 2, and water supply projects such as Ulu Tutong Dam Project.",""],[1,"99","1","Water Supply System Construction, Repair, and Upgrade","the construction / repair / upgrading of the Water Supply system, including the replacement of the main pipes and the construction of water tanks;",""],[1,"121","7","Agis-Agis Treatment Plant Upgrade","Upgrading of Agis-Agis Treatment Plant, Belait District",""],[1,"121","8","National Water Pipe Replacement Programme","Replacement of Old Main Water Pipes throughout the Country",""],[1,"121","9","Water Supply Pipeline Replacement to Sultan Flight Water Tanks","Replacement of Water Supply Pipeline towards Sultan Flight Water Tanks",""],[1,"121","10","Replacement of Main Raw Water Pipe Support","Replacement of New Main Raw Water Pipe Support from Badas Water Pump Station to Seria Water Treatment Plant",""],[1,"121","11","Water Distribution Pipe Replacement Programme","Replacement of Old Water Pipes Asbestos Cement / Galvanized Iron and PVC in Water Distribution System Network",""],[1,"121","12","Water Supply System Improvement Project","Improvement of Water Supply System (Construction of Water Tank and Improvement of Water Pump System)",""]],"22":[[1,"119","17","11kV/415V Network System Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv / 415v Network System at Gadong Power Station 2 to Old Airport New Main Switching 11kv, Brunei and Muara District",""],[1,"119","19","11kV/415V Network System Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv / 415v Network System for Jalan Pasar Gadong and Surrounding Areas",""],[1,"119","1","11kV Network System Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Network System for Jalan Pantai Sg. Liang, Sg. Lalit, Agis-Agis, Sg. Taring Lumut and Surrounding Areas in Belait District",""],[1,"119","3","11kV Network System Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Network System at Sinarubai, Masin, Ban Kampong Mulaut and Surrounding Areas",""],[1,"119","21","11kV Network System Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Network System for Jalan Gadong including Beribi Industry, Jalan Telanai, Kampong Beribi Commercial Area and Surrounding Areas",""],[1,"119","23","Reinforcement of the 11kV Network System","Reinforcement of New 11kv Network System for 11kv Alternative Line from 66 / 11kv Beribi Electricity Station to Batu 1 Jalan Tutong and Batu 3 Main Electricity Station, Daerah Brunei Muara",""],[1,"119","8","11kV Distribution Network Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Distribution Network System Overhead Wire 3c/300mcm from Telisai to Kampong. Sg. Liang and Surrounding Areas in Tutong District",""],[1,"119","9","11kV Distribution Network Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Distribution Network System Overhead Wire 3c/300mcm for Mukim Kiudang and Lamunin including Batu 18 Area to Lamunin, Tutong District",""],[1,"119","10","11kV Distribution Network Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Distribution Network System Overhead Wire 3c/300mcm for Kampong Senukoh, Kampong Piasau-Piasau, Kampong Kenua, Kampong Semabat and Surrounding Areas of Temburong District",""],[1,"119","12","11kV Distribution Network System Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv Distribution Network System Overhead Wire 3c/300mcm throughout Jalan Tutong from Batu 18 to Kampong Keriam, Daerah Tutong",""],[1,"119","2","11kV Power Line Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kv from Rimba Landless MIS to Royal Pavilion MIS, Rimba Resettlement MIS to Royal Pavilion MIS and from Royal Pavilion MIS to Rimba Phase 5 MIS",""],[1,"119","4","11 kV Network System Reinforcement at Badas Area","Reinforcement of 11kv Network System at Badas Area",""],[1,"119","5","Nationwide 415V Low Voltage System Reinforcement Phase 1","Reinforcement of 415v Low Voltage System throughout the Country Phase 1",""],[1,"119","6","11kV Network Reinforcement for Manggis Main Electricity Station","Reinforcement of 11kv Network System for Manggis Main Electricity Station 66kv/11kv to Main National Electricity Station including Jalan Kebangsaan, Delima, Pulaie and Anggerek Desa",""],[1,"119","7","11kV Distribution Network Reinforcement at Diplomatic Area","Reinforcement of 11kv Distribution Network System at Diplomatic Area (Kuwait, Korea, China, Oman and India Embassy)",""],[1,"119","11","Kampong Ayer Electricity Network Reinforcement Phase 1","Reinforcement of 11kv / 415v for Kampong Ayer Phase 1",""],[1,"119","13","11kV Reinforcement from Pasir Puteh Substation","Reinforcement of 11kv from 66kv/11kv Pasir Puteh Substation to JKR Package Unit Sarambangun, Mukim Tanjung Maya and Surrounding Areas in Tutong District",""],[1,"119","14","11kV Power Network Reinforcement in Mukim Pekan Tutong","Reinforcement of 11kv for Mukim Pekan Tutong including Kampong Penanjong, Tanah Buruk, Padang Kawat, Bukit Bendera and Sengkarai",""],[1,"119","15","National Street Lighting Installation Programme","Installation of New Street Lighting throughout the country",""],[1,"119","16","Reinforcement of 11kV/415V Network System","Reinforcement of 11kv / 415v Network System Main Switch Station Jangsak#1, Jangsak#2 to Main Switch Station Beribi VIP Housing from 66 / 11kv Batu 8 Kilanas Substation",""],[1,"119","18","11kV Network System Reinforcement in Kuala Belait District","Reinforcement of 11kv Network System at Kuala Belait District Station: Setia Diraja, Panaga, Kampong Pandan and Rasau Main Network",""],[1,"119","20","Electricity Station Switchgear Upgrading","Upgrading of 11kv 1250a Metalclad Switchgear for Universiti Brunei Darussalam Electricity Station, Gadong Power Station #1, Royal Pavillion, Rimba Resettlement, Kiarong S1, Kiulap 1 and Beribi Industries #1",""],[1,"119","22","Upgrade of 11kV 1250A Metalclad Switchgear","Upgrading of 11kv 1250a Metalclad Switchgear for Layong, Kampong Penanjung, Perpindahan Bukit Beruang and Serambangun Light Industry Main Electricity Station",""],[1,"120","1","Renew and Upgrade Power Generation at Lumut","Renew and Upgrade of Power Generation - Lumut",""],[1,"120","2","High Voltage Circuit Overhead Wire Transmission Project","High Voltage Circuit- Overhead Wire from Lumut Power Station to S/S Setia Di Raja Kuala Belait including Lumut and S/S kV Setia Di Raja (Lumut-Mumong By-Pass)",""],[1,"120","3","High Voltage Circuit Upgrade for Gadong Feeder 7 and 8","High Voltage Circuit- Gadong Feeder 7 & 8 Overhead Wire 275kV from S/S Pasir Puteh to Lumut Power Station",""],[1,"120","4","66/11kV Substation and High Voltage Circuit Construction","High Voltage Circuit- 66/11kV New Substation at Kampong Lugu STKRJ and 66/11kV High Voltage Circuit from Bukit Panggal Power Station to S/S 66/11Kv Kampong Lugu",""],[1,"120","6","Electrical Services Supply Network Asset and Inventory Management","Department of Electrical Services Supply Network Asset/ Inventory Management including Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition Sistem (SCADA)",""],[1,"120","7","66kV Transmission Line Upgrade between GPS#1 and Muara Substation","Upgrading of 66kV Transmission Overhead Line between GPS#1 and Muara 66kV S/S",""],[1,"120","8","Brunei Muara District Electricity Network Reinforcement","Reinforcement of 11kV/415V Brunei Muara District - 66/11kV Manggis Substation to Kampong Subok Spg 546 MIS Gurkha Reserves, Kampong Sg Akar, MIS Kebangsaan 11kV, MIS Kebangsaan 11kV including additional network",""],[1,"120","9","11kV Network System Reinforcement and Main Switch Station Upgrade","Reinforcement of 11KV Network System Main Switch Station Belingus to Propose Main Switch Station 66KV/11KV Perdayan",""],[1,"120","10","66kV Network Circuit Expansion to Perdayan New Stations","Propose 66KV Network Circuit from 66 / 11KV Mentiri Main Stations to New Stations 66/11KV Perdayan, Temburong District",""],[1,"124","5","Construction of New Electricity Substation for Industrial Sites","Construction of New Electricity Substation for Industrial Sites",""]],"23":[[1,"66","2","New Business and Industry Creation Initiative","The anticipated priority initiatives include attracting more FDI, exploring potential PPP programmes, intensifying the development of Government-Linked Companies (GLCs), creating new businesses or industries, enhancing entrepreneurial activities and strengthening MSMEs.",""],[1,"66","2","Entrepreneurship and MSME Strengthening Programme","The anticipated priority initiatives include attracting more FDI, exploring potential PPP programmes, intensifying the development of Government-Linked Companies (GLCs), creating new businesses or industries, enhancing entrepreneurial activities and strengthening MSMEs.",""],[1,"70","4","Private Non-Oil and Gas Sector Diversification Policies and Strategies","the Long-Term Development Plan (2007-2035) ensures that policies, strategies and planning that increases the contribution of the private Non-Oil and Gas Sector to GDP, exports and Government revenue continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"70","4","Private Sector Development Including Government-Linked Companies","the country has to focus on the development of the private sector (including Government Linked-Ccompanies (GLCs)) to help fulfill the goal of increasing revenue or the country's wealth while diversifying the economy at the same time.",""],[1,"70","5","Integrated Economic Diversification Initiatives","Increasing the output of the Non-Oil and Gas Sector requires all parties to implement initiatives to achieve the goal of economic diversification in an integrated manner.",""],[1,"70","5","Private Sector Governance Improvement for Business Processes","Strengthening the private sector through improving public governance, particularly in processes relevant to businesses, will help in attracting foreign direct investment as well as accelerate the growth of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[1,"70","5","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction Measures","Strengthening the private sector through improving public governance, particularly in processes relevant to businesses, will help in attracting foreign direct investment as well as accelerate the growth of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[1,"70","5","MSME Growth Acceleration Support","Strengthening the private sector through improving public governance, particularly in processes relevant to businesses, will help in attracting foreign direct investment as well as accelerate the growth of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[1,"71","1","Business Environment Improvement for Private Sector Growth","Overall, a conducive business environment is also much needed to support the growth of the private sector.",""],[1,"110","2","Ease of Doing Business Regulatory Reform","In ensuring the Government's pro-business governance in line with the 'Ease of Doing Business' (EODB) initiatives, the Government had undertaken reforms to the laws and regulations, and reviewed processes to facilitate business in the country.",""],[1,"111","1","Business Environment Improvement Initiative","Therefore, the country will continue to intensify and strengthen governance in the public sector to support efforts towards enhancing the conducive business environment.",""],[1,"111","2","Business Facilitation Reforms","This achievement involves several reforms and improvements to processes, regulations or legislation, specificially in obtaining electricity, obtaining credit, and tax payments.",""],[1,"111","4","Public Service Delivery Improvement Initiative","The improvement in the quality of public service delivery is aimed to support a more conducive business and investment environment which will generate more economic activities and attracting FDI into the country.",""],[1,"112","1","Service Improvement for Business Process Support","The Government will continue to evaluate and strengthen their respective services to support the needs of the private sector as well as the public sector for seamless and effective business processes.",""],[1,"113","2","Business-Facilitating Legal and Regulatory Reform","amendments to laws and regulations, and updating processes to facilitate business in this country.",""]],"24":[[1,"70","5","Productivity, Innovation, and Technology Transfer Promotion","This will also help to improve productivity, encourage research and innovation, including the introduction of new technology and knowledge transfer.",""],[1,"106","11","Technology-Driven Productivity Improvement Projects","priority is also given to projects that can ensure improvements in productivity through the use of technology.",""],[1,"110","2","Capacity Building for Business Services through Information Technology","the projects under RKN11 is expected to support the continous efforts such as capacity building projects through information technology for example Halal Certification System and Brunei's National Business Services Platform.",""]],"26":[[1,"110","1","Public Sector Governance Strengthening","it is also important to strengthen the governance in the public sector by improving the existing policies and processes.",""],[1,"111","1","Public Sector Governance Strengthening","Therefore, the country will continue to intensify and strengthen governance in the public sector to support efforts towards enhancing the conducive business environment.",""],[1,"110","1","Whole-of-Nation Public-Private Coordination Approach","to support the implementation of RKN11 through the 'Whole of Nation Approach' which needs the participation and coordination between the public sector and the private sector.",""],[1,"110","1","Public Service Integrity and Conduct Development","Some of the aspects needed to produce public service servants with integrity towards realizing robust governance, is the practice of honourable virtues such as honest and trustworthy; efficient, quick and accurate; patient, perseverant and polite.",""],[1,"94","2","Stakeholder Collaboration for Community Mindset Shift","All stakeholders need to carry out their respective roles to shift the community's mindset to be more independent, motivated, hardworking and productive towards contributing to the socio-economic development of the country.",""],[1,"94","2","Pro-Business and Pro-Investment Collaboration Framework","Cohesive collaboration, coupled with continuous support and the involvement of all stakeholders are essential towards developing a more pro-business and pro-investment country.",""]],"27":[[1,"118","7","Slope Protection and Road Upgrading at Batang Duri Camp","Slope Protection and Upgrading Roads, Outward Bound Brunei Darussalam (OBBD), at Batang Duri Camp, Temburong",""],[1,"118","11","New Medical Reception Station at Bolkiah Garrison","Proposed New Medical Reception Station (MRS) Bolkiah Garrison- Balance of Work",""],[1,"118","15","Brunei Embassy and Official Residence Construction in Riyadh","Building for Brunei Embassy and Official Residence in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia",""],[1,"118","16","Rebuilding of the Official Residence of the Brunei High Commissioner in Kuala Lumpur","Rebuilding of Official Residence of Brunei High Commissioner in Kuala Lumpur (Seri Brunei), Malaysia",""],[1,"118","18","Brunei Embassy and Official Residence Upgrade in Brussels","Upgrading of Brunei Embassy and Official Residence in Brussels, Belgium",""],[1,"118","19","Upgrading of Kampong Pulaie Welfare Home","Upgrading of Kampong Pulaie Welfare Home",""]],"28":[[1,"45","1","Project Assessment by Wawasan Champions","every project requested by Ministries will be assessed by the Wawasan Champions beforehand in terms of its relevancy towards achieving Wawasan Brunei 2035 and its effectiveness through its contribution towards the National Outcomes.",""],[1,"26","9","Project Implementation Readiness and Capacity Strengthening","All proposed projects should be ready to be implemented and can be completed within the RKN11.",""],[1,"53","12","Project Implementation Study Within Approved Allocation","any project that required additional funding will be advised to implement detailed and innovative study on how the project will be implemented within the approved allocation without affecting the main function of the project;",""]],"29":[[1,"43","2","Service Delivery Improvement Programme","improvement in the quality of service delivery",""],[1,"19","3","Institutional Capacity Building Programme","As such, priorities will continue to focus on building institutional capacity, development of human resource capital and developing our industries and expand trade network.",""]],"31":[[1,"26","1","Welfare Policy Reform and New Policy Development","the Government sector needs to take pro- active actions in implementing reforms on existing welfares and policies or introducing appropriate new policies.",""]],"32":[[1,"55","2","School Building Construction and Upgrading Projects","These positive developments will continue to be further enhanced during the RKN11, by introducing new programmes to produce highly-skilled and educated people such as the Civil Service Leadership Pipeline (CSLP), Human Resource Fund as well as projects for building, upgrading and construction of school buildings in the country.",""],[1,"42","5","Education Infrastructure Construction and Management System Improvement","the related RKN11 projects includes new and additional construction of buildings and infrastructure, improvement to the national education management system in addition to the provision of human resource development fund and scholarships.",""]],"34":[[1,"25","5","Manpower Planning Aligned with Industry Requirements","This thrust gives emphasis towards manpower planning in line with the industry requirements.",""],[1,"42","3","Integrated Human Capital Development","For this purpose, an integrated human capital development will require improving the education and training system as a whole, encompassing Pre-school, Primary and Secondary Schools, Technical and Vocational Education, Higher Education as well as Lifelong Learning.",""],[1,"42","4","Education and Workforce Training Quality Improvement","There needs to be a shift in focus on education and training needs, from developing physical infrastructure aspects to improving the quality of the education and training of the workforce.",""],[1,"19","3","Human Resource Capital Development Programme","As such, priorities will continue to focus on building institutional capacity, development of human resource capital and developing our industries and expand trade network.",""]],"36":[[1,"55","2","Civil Service Leadership Pipeline Programme","These positive developments will continue to be further enhanced during the RKN11, by introducing new programmes to produce highly-skilled and educated people such as the Civil Service Leadership Pipeline (CSLP), Human Resource Fund as well as projects for building, upgrading and construction of school buildings in the country.",""],[1,"36","3","Brunei Entrepreneurship Education Scheme","Brunei Entrepreneurship Education Scheme / Program Skim Pendidikan Keusahawanan Brunei",""]],"39":[[1,"43","2","Security and Intelligence Capacity Strengthening","strengthening the capabilities of security and intelligence agencies, especially towards ensuring national security",""]],"40":[[1,"43","2","Quality Public Infrastructure and Basic Utilities Development","development and provision of quality public infrastructure and basic utilities",""]],"43":[[1,"66","2","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction Initiative","The anticipated priority initiatives include attracting more FDI, exploring potential PPP programmes, intensifying the development of Government-Linked Companies (GLCs), creating new businesses or industries, enhancing entrepreneurial activities and strengthening MSMEs.",""],[1,"19","3","Industry Development and Trade Network Expansion","As such, priorities will continue to focus on building institutional capacity, development of human resource capital and developing our industries and expand trade network.",""],[1,"26","2","Private Sector Support for MSME Competitiveness and International Market Access","the private sector plays a crucial role in assisting the micro, small and medium sized companies to thrive and be more competitive with other companies from abroad and correspondingly, penetrate the international market.",""],[1,"26","2","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction for Non-Oil and Gas Sector Growth","The influx of Foreign Direct Investments (FDIs) in the country will also accelerate the growth of Non-Oil and Gas Sector and benefit the country, such as through the introduction of new technology, knowledge transfer as well as increase productivity and skilled workforce.",""]],"44":[[1,"26","3","Pro-Business Governance Improvement","The Sixth Thrust is Strengthening Government's Governance for a Conducive Business Environment.",""],[1,"66","2","Government-Linked Companies Development Initiative","The anticipated priority initiatives include attracting more FDI, exploring potential PPP programmes, intensifying the development of Government-Linked Companies (GLCs), creating new businesses or industries, enhancing entrepreneurial activities and strengthening MSMEs.",""],[1,"20","1","Non-Oil and Gas Sector Capacity Strengthening","RKN11's primarily focuses on increasing the capacity of the Non-Oil and Gas Sector by emphasising on strengthening the efficiency in governance, development of a skilled, able and resilient workforce and improving the dynamism of the private sector including local businesses.",""]],"45":[[1,"66","2","Economic Diversification and Non-Oil Sector Growth Strategy","The situation calls for immediate and integrated efforts to be enhanced to diversify economic activities and resources, so as to achieve economic growth that is more sustainable and progressive.",""]],"47":[[1,"50","9","Transportation Infrastructure Construction and Modernisation Projects","Projects under this sector included the construction of Raja Isteri Pengiran Anak Hajah Saleha Bridge, modernisation of the Brunei International Airport, the construction of Tutong Road to Seria, Stage 3 - Road connecting Telisai Lumut (16km) and Temburong Bridge.",""],[1,"55","1","Continuation of Growth-Generating Infrastructure Projects","Similar projects will be continued to be implemented focusing on projects that can generate economic growth.",""]],"50":[[1,"27","2","Public-Private Partnership Financing for Commercial Projects","The Government will also explore the use of alternative financing for projects that have a commercial value in order to encourage private sector involvement in the development of the economy through the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model.",""],[1,"66","2","Public-Private Partnership Programme Exploration","The anticipated priority initiatives include attracting more FDI, exploring potential PPP programmes, intensifying the development of Government-Linked Companies (GLCs), creating new businesses or industries, enhancing entrepreneurial activities and strengthening MSMEs.",""],[1,"61","9","Corporatisation and Commercialisation Review of Government Agencies and Activities","Assessing the possible corporatisation and commercialisation of several agencies or activities that are currently being carried out by Government agencies.",""]],"51":[[1,"78","1","Teacher Capacity Development Initiative","In line with the Government's continuous initiatives to build the capacity of the country's youth, efforts to produce competent, professional and highly motivated teachers will also be emphasised.",""],[1,"78","1","School Leadership Strengthening Initiative","Moreover, the aspect of leadership in schools will also be emphasised to enhance the effectiveness of the education system in Brunei Darussalam.",""],[1,"79","2","Continuous Professional Development Programme for Teachers","One initiative is the continuous professional development programme through the Brunei Darussalam Teachers Academy (BDTA).",""],[1,"79","2","Teachers Professional Development Framework","The Teachers Professional Development Framework is another programme implemented which looks to develop professional teachers in a systematic process and aims to create and increase the effectiveness of efforts to develop 'professional learning communities' among teachers and school leaders.",""],[1,"79","3","Teacher-Workplace Trainer Partnership Programme","the Teacher-Workplace Trainer Partnership Programme is also carried out for teachers in fields related to oil and gas",""],[1,"80","1","School Leadership Development Programmes","Leadership programmes will also continue to be implemented to produce skilled school leaders.",""],[1,"93","5","Teacher Professional Development and Recruitment","as well as competent, professional and highly-skilled teachers",""]],"52":[[1,"77","2","Overseas Higher Education Scholarship Scheme","Students also have the opportunity to pursue their studies in higher learning institutions overseas through scholarships and the Government's Education Financing Scheme",""],[1,"89","1","Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme","the Government has prepared a scholarship scheme i.e. Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme (BPTV) under the RKN specifically for 'O' level graduates to further their studies in private educational institutions.",""]],"53":[[1,"81","1","National Entrepreneurship Agenda","the National Entrepreneurship Agenda (NEA) is also being undertaken.",""],[1,"81","1","Brunei Entrepreneurship Education Scheme 2.0","the Brunei Entrepreneurship Education Scheme (BEES) 2.0 is another programme being implemented which aims to assist students to better understand business methods through practical activities, creating awareness for self-reliance, as well as by inspiring youths to learn and understand business concepts.",""],[1,"92","4","Entrepreneurship Specialisation Development","Therefore, towards building this visionary and 'Wasatiah' community, specialisation in the field of entrepreneurship is key.",""],[1,"94","1","Youth Business and Entrepreneurship Knowledge Initiative","initiatives to enhance knowledge, among the local youth and community, in the field of business and entrepreneurship are also given attention especially among the youth who has the potential, where project such as Youth Development Centre (PPB) is provided.",""]],"54":[[1,"89","2","Creative and Multimedia Industry Training Programmes","training programmes in the creative and multimedia industry are provided by the iCentre, Knowledge Hub and Design and Technology Centre.",""]],"55":[[1,"98","4","Community Facilities and Basic Utilities Upgrade Project","RKN11 projects will encompass the provision and upgrading of facilities and basic utilities as well as the improvement of public safety through the supply of electricity and water, housing, medical services, roads, bridges, and others.",""],[1,"104","7","Basic Infrastructure Support through RKN10 Projects","Some of the developments in the above subsectors are supported by the provision of basic infrastructure implemented through RKN10 projects.",""]],"56":[[1,"99","1","Government Asset Maintenance and Repair Programme","the Government will continuously carry out maintenance and repairs on Government assets.",""],[1,"99","1","Public Building Maintenance and Library Upgrade Programme","Maintenance and repairs of existing buildings, housing including houses constructed under National Housing Scheme and to upgrade library buildings in Bandar Seri Begawan;",""]],"57":[[1,"100","2","Crime Prevention and Law Enforcement Strengthening","With regards to the quality of life, I want the relevant authorities to be more agile and efficient in handling the rising crime rates, which has been occurring since the past few years.",""],[1,"100","4","Police Force Academy","specific projects will be carried out, including the Police Force Academy, Brunei National Cyber Security Framework and National Emergency Response System (NERS).",""]],"58":[[1,"100","4","Brunei National Cyber Security Framework","specific projects will be carried out, including the Police Force Academy, Brunei National Cyber Security Framework and National Emergency Response System (NERS).",""],[1,"100","4","National Emergency Response System","specific projects will be carried out, including the Police Force Academy, Brunei National Cyber Security Framework and National Emergency Response System (NERS).",""]],"59":[[1,"120","18","Replacement and Enhancement of Weather Radar Network","Replacement and Enhancement of Meteorological Department Weather Radar Network",""],[1,"120","20","Airport Automatic Weather Observation System Replacement","Replacement of Airport Automatic Weather Observation System (AWOS) at Brunei International Airport",""],[1,"120","21","Instrument Landing System and DVOR/DME Replacement","Provision of Replacement of Instrument Landing System (ILS) and Doppler VHM Omni Directional Range /Distance Measuring Equipment (DVOR / DME)",""],[1,"121","5","Muara Radio Signal Station Enhancement","➢ Enhancement of Muara Radio Signal Station",""],[1,"122","13","FM Radio Transmission Equipment Replacement","Replacement of FM Radio Transmission Equipment System at Bukit Subok Station and Andulau Transmission Station",""],[1,"122","14","CORS Upgrading and Densification","Upgrading & Densification of Continuously Operating Reference Station (CORS)",""]],"60":[[1,"121","2","Construction of Retention Basins in Sungai Tutong Catchment","Construction of Retention Basins in Sungai Tutong Catchment",""],[1,"121","3","Upgrading and Desilting of Major Rivers and Tributaries","Upgrading and Desilting of Major Rivers and Tributaries",""],[1,"121","20","Flood Mitigation Pond Construction, Tutong District Phase I","Construction of Flood Mitigation Pond Daerah Tutong - Phase I",""],[1,"121","21","Tutong River Flood Mitigation Scheme","Flood Mitigation Scheme at Tutong River",""]],"61":[[1,"123","2","BRU-HIMS Enhancement","➢ Enhancement of BRU-HIMS",""]],"62":[[1,"106","10","Brunei Stock Exchange Establishment","the establishment of the Brunei Stock Exchange to support the growth of Financial Subsector in Brunei Darussalam",""],[1,"124","1","Brunei Darussalam Stock Exchange Establishment Project","Establishment of Brunei Darussalam Stock Exchange Project",""]],"63":[[1,"106","10","Tourism Product Strengthening Initiative","strengthening of tourism products",""],[1,"124","11","Upgrading of the Old Customs Building Art Gallery","Upgrading of Art Gallery Building (Old Customs Building)",""],[1,"124","12","Brunei Museum Building and Exhibition Building Rehabilitation and Upgrading","Rehabilitation and Upgrading of Brunei Museum Building and Exhibition Building, Kota Batu",""],[1,"124","13","Kampong Ayer Tourism Products and Packages Strengthening","Strengthening of Kampong Ayer Tourism Products and Packages",""]],"64":[[1,"105","3","Private Sector High-Value Product and Service Development","the RKN projects were also expected to nurture the ability of the private sector to produce varieties of high value and innovative products and services",""]]}});